{1000}{490c Facts Revealed About Jack The Riddler!}
{1001}{483l    This week marks the one year anniversary of the first of many brutal murders in our fair city. Despite the tireless efforts of local and national law enforcement agencies using the latest investigatory techniques and technology, little is known about the elusive and mysterious murderer. Even less is known by the public at large. Naturally, this lack of factual information has led to widespread gossip and unsubstantiated rumors. This sort of thing has done more harm then good, causing an already concerned and frightened city ever more turmoil. It is therefore my sincere hope to finally put to rest these harmful untruths and bring to light some facts about the ongoing case.}
{1002}{483l    Yesterday I had the very special privilege of interviewing the person responsible for profiling the mysterious murderer. Retired Detective Lord Davidian needs no introduction. His thirty years of distinguished service with Yotland Scard has made him a national hero. He was responsible for an amazing seventy-two per cent of federal arrests in our city and forty-three per cent nationwide. He has received numerous awards and citations during his illustrious career including the Mayor's Citation of Merit, the Royal Cross, the Outstanding Service Award and, upon his recent retirement, the well-deserved title of Lordship from H.R.M. A warning to our readers before I continue: portions of the following interview may be unsettling to some.
TW: "First of all I want to thank you for taking a few moments of what must be a taxing and troublesome case."
LD: "Oh, it's my pleasure. I've been hoping to quill the rumors which have plagued the city's citizens for so long."
TW: "A year ago today a woman, a prostitute to be exact, was found face up sprawled on the ground in an alley murdered..."
LD: "Yes, that was the first of many such murders."
TW: "And a Const. Calis discovered the body. He reported that the victim's throat was slit and her heart was removed from her body with a scalpel "as if done by a surgeon". I believe those were his exact words? And Const. Calis has aided in the ongoing investigation from that moment?
LD: "Right. A dreadful bit of business that. Const. Calis has been of invaluable assistance to our investigation."
TW: "So, is it safe to say that your immediate primary suspect was...}
{1003}{483c - CONTINUED ON PAGE A-4 - }

{1010}{490c Jack The Riddler Claims 5th Victim!}
{1011}{483l    In the early hours of this very morning, the deceased body of Mrs. Ruth Knaksbee was found lying in an alley of Olde Town Square. As is the gruesome signature of Jack The Riddler, a vital organ (in this case the heart) was carefully extracted via sharp, precise cuts like those made by a scalpel. Likewise, a note from the assailant was found pinned to the young woman's soiled and disheveled dress. Authorities would not reveal the contents of the note, but did say that it provided some clue as to where Jack The Riddler may strike next.}
{1012}{483l    On a similar note, Yotland Scard Special Branch, the lead law inforcement agency on the case of Jack The Riddler, is expecting their newest Detective today to help fill the vacancy left by former detectives who mysteriously disappeared over the past year. In this reporters opinion, much more is needed in the way of manpower and resources if these brutal and senseless murders are ever to cease and the loved ones of the victims ever to see justice served against Jack The Riddler.}
{1013}{492c _ PICNIC FUNDRAISER _}
{1014}{483l The Fellowship Of Church Restorers will be holding a public picnic fundraiser this Saturday starting 12:00 pm in Heroman Park. The funds are to go to the ongoing restoration of Our Lady Of Eternal Sorrow church in New Town Square. All are encouraged to attend and various recreational activities are planned.}
{1015}{492c _ EDITORIAL REMINDER _}
{1016}{483l The Nodnol Times would like to take this opportunity to remind its gentle readers that all letters to the editor do not necessarily reflect the views of this newspaper or its owner, Mr. Deathy.}
{1017}{492c _ WEATHER _}
{1018}{483l The Meteorological Service Bureau of Nodnol is predicting sunny weather for the next two to three days, with an increasing chance of precipitation before the passage of a Fortnight.}
